// Goat OS staging Grafana Alloy configuration (Faro RUM direct to GCP).
//
// Deployed as the container config for the `goatos-stg-grafana-alloy` Cloud
// Run service (infra/envs/stg/observability.tf, asia-south1). Alloy's job
// here is narrow: terminate browser Real User Monitoring (RUM) telemetry from
// admin-web's `@grafana/faro-web-sdk` and forward it directly to GCP Cloud
// Trace using workload identity. See docs/observability/FARO_RUM.md and
// OBSERVABILITY_DESIGN.md section 2.4.
//
// ARCHITECTURE CHANGE: Alloy exports directly to Google Cloud (no sidecar
// collector). The Faro receiver accepts CORS-restricted POST payloads from
// browsers, parses them into OTLP traces, and forwards to
// otelcol.exporter.googlecloud. Workload identity (service account binding)
// handles authentication — no API keys are present.
//
// NOTE (v1 limitation): Faro's log output is in Loki format, not OTLP format,
// so logs cannot be sent to the OTLP-based googlecloud exporter. In v2, logs
// can be forwarded via loki.write or a format adapter. For this pass, RUM
// visibility comes from browser traces (page loads, JS errors, web vitals).
// Log-to-metrics transforms can be added in Cloud Logging later.

// Faro receiver: HTTP endpoint the browser SDK POSTs RUM payloads to.
// admin-web's faro-web-sdk `url` config points at this Cloud Run service's
// public HTTPS endpoint (Alloy runs with INGRESS_TRAFFIC_ALL — see
// observability.tf — because browsers must reach it).
//
// SECURITY: cors_allowed_origins is restricted to the real admin-web origin
// to prevent malicious websites from flooding the RUM sink with fake telemetry.
// If the stg domain changes, update both this list and the admin-web SDK
// configuration. Rate limiting is enforced at the Cloud Run service level
// (Cloud Armor policy) as a residual defense; this config-level CORS
// restriction is the first-line filter. See docs/observability/INFRA.md.
faro.receiver "admin_web_rum" {
  server {
    listen_address       = "0.0.0.0"
    listen_port          = 8080
    cors_allowed_origins = ["https://stg.dashboard.mesha.sg"]
  }

  output {
    // Traces go to the Google Cloud exporter (OTLP format).
    // Logs are in Loki format and require separate handling;
    // for now, we focus on RUM traces. Cloud Logging support
    // can be added via loki.write or similar in a future pass.
    traces = [otelcol.exporter.googlecloud.default.input]
  }
}

// Google Cloud exporter: traces and logs flow directly to Cloud Trace and
// Cloud Logging. Workload identity (service account binding) provides auth.
// Project ID is read from the metadata service (no explicit config needed).
//
// The Cloud Run service account (goatos-grafana-alloy-stg) must have:
// - roles/cloudtrace.agent (for Cloud Trace writes)
// - roles/logging.logWriter (for Cloud Logging writes)
otelcol.exporter.googlecloud "default" {
  project = ""  // auto-detect from GCP metadata service

  metric {
    prefix = "custom.googleapis.com"
  }
}
